Group by a nested intrinsic (`by(event:name)`). Reference Tempo groups
spans by event name; cerberus groups on the per-span Events.Name Nested
array column so /api/search returns 2xx. SQL/chplan-only golden.

-- query.traceql --
{ } | by(event:name)
-- args --
[0] int64 = 1
[1] bool = true
-- chplan --
Aggregate groupBy=[TraceId AS TraceId, Events.Name AS GroupKey] funcs=[FnAny(SpanId) AS SpanId, FnCount(1) AS Value, FnAny(SpanName) AS MetricName, FnAny(ResourceAttributes) AS ResourceAttrs, FnAny(ParentSpanId) AS ParentSpanId, FnMin(Timestamp) AS TimeUnix, FnMin(FnToUnixNanos(Timestamp)) AS TraceStartNs, FnMax((FnToUnixNanos(Timestamp) + FnToInt64(Duration))) AS TraceEndNs]
  Filter predicate=true
    Scan(otel_traces)
-- sql --
SELECT `TraceId` AS `TraceId`, `Events.Name` AS `GroupKey`, any(`SpanId`) AS `SpanId`, toFloat64(count(?)) AS `Value`, any(`SpanName`) AS `MetricName`, any(`ResourceAttributes`) AS `ResourceAttrs`, any(`ParentSpanId`) AS `ParentSpanId`, min(`Timestamp`) AS `TimeUnix`, min(toUnixTimestamp64Nano(`Timestamp`)) AS `TraceStartNs`, max((toUnixTimestamp64Nano(`Timestamp`) + toInt64(`Duration`))) AS `TraceEndNs` FROM (SELECT * FROM `otel_traces` WHERE ?) GROUP BY `TraceId`, `GroupKey`
-- parity_exempt --
reason: emitted-sql-only
detail: `{ } | by(event:name)` carries no `seed:` or `expected_rows:` — it pins the emitted SQL for this shape, and executes no answer for any oracle to compare
